01:01:36.527 --> 01:01:38.314
- It's a learning experience.

01:01:38.314 --> 01:01:39.469
- Yeah, it's a learning experience.

01:01:39.469 --> 01:01:40.955
And I feel like in any other situation,

01:01:40.955 --> 01:01:42.880
people would call what
I went through, abuse.

01:01:42.880 --> 01:01:46.226
But like, you go in like
with the possibility

01:01:46.226 --> 01:01:48.487
of going to the military
and you have to be strong.

01:01:48.487 --> 01:01:50.667
So in order to do that,
you're pushed to your limits.

01:01:50.667 --> 01:01:51.738
- I've met some people who joined

01:01:51.738 --> 01:01:52.899
because they felt like they needed

01:01:52.899 --> 01:01:55.439
someone to like guide them,

01:01:55.439 --> 01:01:57.873
like tell them what to do
and get their shit together.

01:01:57.873 --> 01:01:59.598
- Pretty much, and it's not for someone

01:01:59.598 --> 01:02:02.183
who doesn't like being told
what to do, I can tell you that.

01:02:02.183 --> 01:02:03.016
- Yeah, obviously.

01:02:03.016 --> 01:02:05.802
- Yeah and the actual Marine Corps base,

01:02:05.802 --> 01:02:07.138
I remember like, you'd wait,

01:02:07.138 --> 01:02:10.086
you'd be yelled at for
pretty much the entire day.

01:02:10.086 --> 01:02:12.591
Then you'd go to bed at
midnight and you get to sleep

01:02:12.591 --> 01:02:13.424
for four hours.

01:02:13.424 --> 01:02:15.015
And that's the only time of
peace that you have to yourself

01:02:15.015 --> 01:02:17.401
and that four in the morning,
the drill instructors,

01:02:17.401 --> 01:02:18.619
like come banging on the door

01:02:18.619 --> 01:02:20.271
and then like rip your sheets off.

01:02:20.271 --> 01:02:21.252
And then they tell you to get up

01:02:21.252 --> 01:02:22.172
and you have to stand at attention,

01:02:22.172 --> 01:02:23.652
but you're like all dizzy and stuff.

01:02:23.652 --> 01:02:27.263
And then by the time I ranked
up to chief petty officer,

01:02:27.263 --> 01:02:29.962
which I guess it's just high ranking.

01:02:29.962 --> 01:02:33.519
I got to be one of the people
to chew out other cadets.

01:02:33.519 --> 01:02:34.934
- That would have been fun.

01:02:34.934 --> 01:02:35.837
- You know what?

01:02:35.837 --> 01:02:37.172
All of that.
- How did that feel?

01:02:37.172 --> 01:02:38.005
- So satisfying.

01:02:38.005 --> 01:02:39.053
(all laughing)

01:02:39.053 --> 01:02:41.431
So, I went through like three
and a half years by this point

01:02:41.431 --> 01:02:42.267
and being yelled at.

01:02:42.267 --> 01:02:43.500
And then now you get to be the person,

01:02:43.500 --> 01:02:44.333
to yell at other people.

01:02:44.333 --> 01:02:46.721
- Its making a bunch of psychopaths.

01:02:46.721 --> 01:02:50.888
