So then, I got these messages

01:10:22.359 --> 01:10:24.158
from like old high
school people like being,

01:10:24.158 --> 01:10:24.991
"You're going?"

01:10:24.991 --> 01:10:25.843
And I'm like, Oh yeah.

01:10:25.843 --> 01:10:26.676
- No, no, I'm just stalking you.

01:10:26.676 --> 01:10:27.724
- Yeah, yeah, I'm just seeing.

01:10:27.724 --> 01:10:29.570
- I just wanna know what you're all up to.

01:10:29.570 --> 01:10:30.888
- I'm just looking, promises, no promises,

01:10:30.888 --> 01:10:31.721
I'm gonna show up.

01:10:31.721 --> 01:10:34.499
- 'Cause I've heard like
there are some high schools

01:10:34.499 --> 01:10:36.339
where like say it, like
they don't have a website,

01:10:36.339 --> 01:10:39.226
where it's literally just someone
from that year being like,

01:10:39.226 --> 01:10:41.910
'I've like booked the pub down the road."

01:10:41.910 --> 01:10:43.418
- That's exactly what
happened in my school.

01:10:43.418 --> 01:10:44.325
- Yeah, exactly.

01:10:44.325 --> 01:10:45.802
- It was literally just a Facebook group

01:10:45.802 --> 01:10:47.027
that everyone got invited to.

01:10:47.027 --> 01:10:49.134
And apparently some people showed up

01:10:49.134 --> 01:10:50.606
and I kind of wish I did.

01:10:50.606 --> 01:10:53.285
- I remember when I was in high school,

01:10:53.285 --> 01:10:54.527
I used to see them on TV all the time,

01:10:54.527 --> 01:10:55.425
high school reunions.

01:10:55.425 --> 01:10:57.482
"I'm like, I don't fucking see anyone.

01:10:57.482 --> 01:10:58.753
"I don't want to meet anyone."

01:10:58.753 --> 01:11:00.741
I'm just like that one
edgy anime characters.

01:11:00.741 --> 01:11:02.335
Like they don't know-

01:11:02.335 --> 01:11:03.331
- They all bullied me back then.

01:11:03.331 --> 01:11:06.098
- They don't know that
I'm 1200 rating in chess.

01:11:06.098 --> 01:11:07.385
I'm kidding but-

01:11:07.385 --> 01:11:08.509
- It's that fucking meme,

01:11:08.509 --> 01:11:10.390
where the guy standing
in the corner being like,

01:11:10.390 --> 01:11:13.223
"They don't know I'm a pray con player."

01:11:13.223 --> 01:11:14.664
(all laughing)

01:11:14.664 --> 01:11:16.373
- For the first three years I was like,

01:11:16.373 --> 01:11:18.755
" Fuck high school reunions,
I'm too cool for that."

01:11:18.755 --> 01:11:20.311
But then more and more, it goes down.

01:11:20.311 --> 01:11:21.144
I'm like, "You know what?

01:11:21.144 --> 01:11:22.352
"I think I'd actually like
to see how everyone's doing.

01:11:22.352 --> 01:11:23.356
- [Joey] Yeah, it'd be nice.

01:11:23.356 --> 01:11:26.488
- I'm genuinely curious,
especially during quarantine,

01:11:26.488 --> 01:11:28.532
I had this weekend when I'm just like,

01:11:28.532 --> 01:11:30.047
"Man, I wonder what everyone's up to.

01:11:30.047 --> 01:11:32.943
'Cause I feel like you get
that day one, like one day.

01:11:32.943 --> 01:11:34.140
- Hire a PI, what would you do?

01:11:34.140 --> 01:11:36.690
- Just like you see what
people were up to on Facebook

01:11:36.690 --> 01:11:38.655
'cause you haven't
talked to them in years.

01:11:38.655 --> 01:11:40.609
They had all these dreams and aspirations.

01:11:40.609 --> 01:11:44.081
You do see some people
who are able to like...

01:11:44.081 --> 01:11:46.850
Some people who have just
been stuck in their hometown.

01:11:46.850 --> 01:11:50.234
- I feel like most people
wanted that, where I grew up.

01:11:50.234 --> 01:11:51.996
I think it was almost expected

01:11:51.996 --> 01:11:54.490
that you never really leave the town.

01:11:54.490 --> 01:11:57.235
- I feel like that's
like a small town mindset

01:11:57.235 --> 01:11:59.205
because I feel like a lot of people,

01:11:59.205 --> 01:12:01.005
I talked to Sidney's family a lot

01:12:01.005 --> 01:12:03.084
and the people living in her town

01:12:03.084 --> 01:12:05.928
and everyone kind of just
stays in that one town.

01:12:05.928 --> 01:12:08.540
And you're kind of like part of a clan.

01:12:08.540 --> 01:12:11.132
And if you leave the clan,
you're like you're banished.

01:12:11.132 --> 01:12:12.331
- You're dishonoring the clan.

01:12:12.331 --> 01:12:13.687
- You're like the one who thought

01:12:13.687 --> 01:12:15.652
you were too good for the lifestyle.

01:12:15.652 --> 01:12:18.119
'Cause nearly like, I think
most people in my family,

01:12:18.119 --> 01:12:21.312
like the old generations
live near the same area,

01:12:21.312 --> 01:12:22.322
like within an hour drive.

01:12:22.322 --> 01:12:24.104
And that's really weird to think about,

01:12:24.104 --> 01:12:27.106
now that everyone lives
within like an hour drive,

01:12:27.106 --> 01:12:28.455
like generations of families.

01:12:28.455 --> 01:12:29.895
So I'm like, "Wait, did
no one have the idea

01:12:29.895 --> 01:12:30.925
"to just like to leave?"

01:12:30.925 --> 01:12:32.842
- I feel like as a kid,

01:12:35.114 --> 01:12:38.004
it's a really like exotic
idea to live somewhere else

01:12:38.004 --> 01:12:39.258
and be somewhere new.

01:12:39.258 --> 01:12:41.585
But then I feel like you underestimate

01:12:41.585 --> 01:12:44.241
just how much you like comfort.

01:12:44.241 --> 01:12:46.491
Like, it really takes a lot

01:12:47.413 --> 01:12:48.246
for someone to be like,

01:12:48.246 --> 01:12:50.689
"I'm going to live in a new country."

01:12:50.689 --> 01:12:53.948
And even for those of us who
live in different countries,

01:12:53.948 --> 01:12:56.223
I know there are a lot
of things about home

01:12:56.223 --> 01:12:57.393
that I'm sure you miss.

01:12:57.393 --> 01:13:00.160
And even if you really like
the place that you live in,

01:13:00.160 --> 01:13:02.109
there's a lot of things you miss as well.

01:13:02.109 --> 01:13:04.068
- Like it's, massive props to like,

01:13:04.068 --> 01:13:06.210
I think all three of our parents, right?

01:13:06.210 --> 01:13:08.796
At least that had the balls to be like,

01:13:08.796 --> 01:13:10.085
I'm just gonna go to this country

01:13:10.085 --> 01:13:11.751
I know fucking nothing about.

01:13:11.751 --> 01:13:15.353
- Yeah, so my parents took
it pretty like easily for me.

01:13:15.353 --> 01:13:17.243
- Yeah, because it's
like Thailand to the UK,

01:13:17.243 --> 01:13:19.070
Philippines to America, and in my case,

01:13:19.070 --> 01:13:20.282
Japan to Australia, right?

01:13:20.282 --> 01:13:22.912
It's like I've always wanted...

01:13:22.912 --> 01:13:24.671
- For me I had like five generations,

01:13:24.671 --> 01:13:26.900
that lived in the same town.

01:13:26.900 --> 01:13:29.318
- Yeah my DNA test is like
a hundred percent British.

01:13:29.318 --> 01:13:30.568
Like there's no one in my family

01:13:30.568 --> 01:13:34.336
who's from any other
country in any like way.

01:13:34.336 --> 01:13:35.859
- Well, because like you also,

01:13:35.859 --> 01:13:37.998
not only will your parents not only moved

01:13:37.998 --> 01:13:39.990
from the Philippines to America,

01:13:39.990 --> 01:13:42.068
but they also moved to
probably the most like

01:13:42.068 --> 01:13:47.046
non-friendly place for like
non-white people, right?

01:13:47.046 --> 01:13:49.869
- So, I was technically born
in Bakersfield, California

01:13:49.869 --> 01:13:51.396
'cause the labor clock was ticking.

01:13:51.396 --> 01:13:52.941
But then as soon as I was born,

01:13:52.941 --> 01:13:57.250
they went to Virginia and
then I lived half my life

01:13:57.250 --> 01:13:59.761
in a place that honestly
sounds like the beginning

01:13:59.761 --> 01:14:02.789
of an RPG game, it's
called Mechanicsville.

01:14:02.789 --> 01:14:04.022
(all laughing)

01:14:04.022 --> 01:14:06.550
It sounds like something
in Ni no Kuni, honestly.

01:14:06.550 --> 01:14:07.383
- Yeah, it's like JLPG name.

01:14:07.383 --> 01:14:08.466
- And then I-

01:14:10.215 --> 01:14:12.010
- Starting village.
- Mechanicsville.

01:14:12.010 --> 01:14:13.315
- what was weird is like,

01:14:13.315 --> 01:14:15.969
I didn't even realize,
I had like this weird,

01:14:15.969 --> 01:14:18.828
I guess almost country twain to my accent

01:14:18.828 --> 01:14:21.563
until I came to the
West coast to Las Vegas.

01:14:21.563 --> 01:14:24.459
And then people were teasing
of like the way I say, y'all

01:14:24.459 --> 01:14:26.700
or the fact that I even say y'all a lot.

01:14:26.700 --> 01:14:28.380
So I had to kind of like-

01:14:28.380 --> 01:14:31.754
- I didn't realize that
Virginia, they say, y'all.

01:14:31.754 --> 01:14:32.587
- Because it doesn't...

01:14:32.587 --> 01:14:33.671
Because you look at it on a map

01:14:33.671 --> 01:14:36.471
and it's like, "Oh, that's
in a Winnie, Texas."

01:14:36.471 --> 01:14:37.377
- Of course, they're not-

01:14:37.377 --> 01:14:39.336
- Texas is not the only in Las Vegas.

01:14:39.336 --> 01:14:41.556
- No but just like someone who
knows nothing about America.

01:14:41.556 --> 01:14:44.296
Like when you hear, y'all,
you immediately think,

01:14:44.296 --> 01:14:45.172
"Oh yeah, Texas."

01:14:45.172 --> 01:14:47.772
- You think southerner,
like that's what I think.

01:14:47.772 --> 01:14:49.281
- Well, like Virginia is
not even in the South.

01:14:49.281 --> 01:14:51.368
It's like kind of halfway
up on the East coast.

01:14:51.368 --> 01:14:54.324
- But it is also kind of
like the founding ground.

01:14:54.324 --> 01:14:56.349
- Yeah, but most people don't know that.

01:14:56.349 --> 01:14:57.661
- No one knows that except me.

01:14:57.661 --> 01:15:01.019
- I know that, I like U.S. history.

01:15:01.019 --> 01:15:01.852
- Oh, really?

01:15:01.852 --> 01:15:02.685
I like-

01:15:02.685 --> 01:15:03.804
- Because there's barely any of it.

01:15:03.804 --> 01:15:04.764
- Oh yeah, that's true.

01:15:04.764 --> 01:15:07.688
Well compared to the UK.
- It's true there's nothing.

01:15:07.688 --> 01:15:09.790
UK history is so fucking confusing.

01:15:09.790 --> 01:15:11.093
- I went through a weird period

01:15:11.093 --> 01:15:13.480
where I was obsessed with you
guys' history and culture.

01:15:13.480 --> 01:15:14.313
- There so much of it.

01:15:14.313 --> 01:15:15.944
- And there's like so
many bands that like,

01:15:15.944 --> 01:15:18.337
I love that none of my friends
in the U.S. can relate to,

01:15:18.337 --> 01:15:20.326
like, I think when we were at karaoke,

01:15:20.326 --> 01:15:22.206
Garnt was so surprised I
was playing Kaiser Chiefs,

01:15:22.206 --> 01:15:24.395
"I Predict a Riot," 'cause
it doesn't seem like,

01:15:24.395 --> 01:15:26.328
or "Take That Shine."

01:15:26.328 --> 01:15:29.159
- Take that, just to give you like my mom

01:15:29.159 --> 01:15:30.890
and her friends love "Take That Shine."

01:15:30.890 --> 01:15:33.158
That's the kind of demos
that they have in the UK.

01:15:33.158 --> 01:15:35.230
- The first time she
was playing "Take That",

01:15:35.230 --> 01:15:36.063
And I saw the music video I was like,

01:15:36.063 --> 01:15:38.841
"Wow, the Backstreet
Boys gone really old."

01:15:38.841 --> 01:15:42.306
- Especially at the UK Backstreet
Boys for middle-aged women

01:15:42.306 --> 01:15:46.223
who are married, kind of
like that target then-

01:15:47.432 --> 01:15:50.227
- (laughs) Yeah, but like,
that's the thing, right?

01:15:50.227 --> 01:15:54.977
It's not until you look deep
into the whole U.S geography

01:15:56.330 --> 01:15:57.163
that you realize that,

01:15:57.163 --> 01:15:59.116
"Oh, just because it's
not in a particular area,

01:15:59.116 --> 01:16:01.830
"it doesn't necessarily mean
they don't talk the same way."

01:16:01.830 --> 01:16:02.663
Like I thought...

01:16:02.663 --> 01:16:03.662
I don't know what I thought

01:16:03.662 --> 01:16:05.243
people in Virginia sounded like,

01:16:05.243 --> 01:16:08.404
I thought maybe they sounded
close to people from New York.

01:16:08.404 --> 01:16:09.440
Yeah, I don't know.

01:16:09.440 --> 01:16:10.618
- New York sounds like it's own thing.

01:16:10.618 --> 01:16:11.988
- I feel like the way,

01:16:11.988 --> 01:16:14.926
like some Americans are
probably hearing this right now

01:16:14.926 --> 01:16:16.847
and being like, and
cringing because I feel like

01:16:16.847 --> 01:16:18.667
the way we talk about American geography,

01:16:18.667 --> 01:16:20.768
is how we feel when we hear Americans

01:16:20.768 --> 01:16:22.720
talk about Europe or something.

01:16:22.720 --> 01:16:25.087
- I think like someone from the UK,

01:16:25.087 --> 01:16:28.351
I think that British accents
and like where that laid out,

01:16:28.351 --> 01:16:30.180
is 20 times more confusing.

01:16:30.180 --> 01:16:31.752
- Oh, 100%.
- I think they are as well.

01:16:31.752 --> 01:16:34.103
- U.S. is so easy to keep
track of where someone's from,

01:16:34.103 --> 01:16:35.051
based on the accent.

01:16:35.051 --> 01:16:36.119
In the UK it's like,

01:16:36.119 --> 01:16:39.186
"Oh, this guy sounds
completely different to person,

01:16:39.186 --> 01:16:41.020
like A person sounds
different from B person.

01:16:41.020 --> 01:16:42.909
They could either be like two hours apart

01:16:42.909 --> 01:16:45.011
or literally five minutes
in a different town.

01:16:45.011 --> 01:16:47.490
- 'Cause, what's confusing
about UK accents,

01:16:47.490 --> 01:16:49.756
is that you can travel
a small enough distance

01:16:49.756 --> 01:16:52.392
and have a widely varied accent.

01:16:52.392 --> 01:16:53.481
- Well, I mean, just in London,

01:16:53.481 --> 01:16:55.091
there's like 20 different accents.

01:16:55.091 --> 01:16:58.989
And that's just a city,
whereas in Australia,

01:16:58.989 --> 01:17:01.547
I think Australia is the
only English-speaking country

01:17:01.547 --> 01:17:04.875
that doesn't have regional
dialects or accents.

01:17:04.875 --> 01:17:07.389
- They just have like
degrees of like strength-

01:17:07.389 --> 01:17:09.491
- Yeah but that's not based on you are,

01:17:09.491 --> 01:17:13.000
that's based on how far
off the coast you are.

01:17:13.000 --> 01:17:14.907
It's like the further inland you are,

01:17:14.907 --> 01:17:16.790
the less you're able to understand them.

01:17:16.790 --> 01:17:18.184
- Its just an Aussie scale basically.

01:17:18.184 --> 01:17:19.516
And you, scale up.

01:17:19.516 --> 01:17:21.667
- You scale up the further inland you go.

01:17:21.667 --> 01:17:22.712
(all laughing)

01:17:22.712 --> 01:17:24.715
It's like, "Oh yeah, you're
definitely from the inland.

01:17:24.715 --> 01:17:26.890
"If I can't understand what
the fuck you're saying,

01:17:26.890 --> 01:17:29.275
because like, you know,
like Kevin for example,

01:17:29.275 --> 01:17:32.052
he's from Perth, which is
all the way on the West coast

01:17:32.052 --> 01:17:33.457
and I'm from the East coast.

01:17:33.457 --> 01:17:37.127
But if you ask someone who
doesn't know Australian accent-

01:17:37.127 --> 01:17:37.960
- Yeah, you do sound the same.
- We would sound

01:17:37.960 --> 01:17:38.793
exactly the same.

01:17:38.793 --> 01:17:39.626
- You two sound exactly the same, yeah.

01:17:39.626 --> 01:17:41.313
- That doesn't work in America at all.

01:17:41.313 --> 01:17:42.146
Like in America,

01:17:42.146 --> 01:17:42.979
you can clearly tell

01:17:42.979 --> 01:17:43.957
if someone's from New
York versus California.

01:17:43.957 --> 01:17:46.581
- You can pinpoint pretty
well, like even like Louisiana

01:17:46.581 --> 01:17:50.264
or like just from Texas to California,

01:17:50.264 --> 01:17:52.311
they just say like a lot.

01:17:52.311 --> 01:17:53.753
Yeah, and I don't know, and-

01:17:53.753 --> 01:17:55.497
- I wonder did your obsession with the UK

01:17:55.497 --> 01:17:56.635
start with the crown?

01:17:56.635 --> 01:17:57.468
Is that why?

01:17:57.468 --> 01:17:58.411
- No, actually way before that.

01:17:58.411 --> 01:17:59.350
- Really?
- Yeah.

01:17:59.350 --> 01:18:00.979
- Sorry to interrupt you.
- No, no, it's cool.

01:18:00.979 --> 01:18:02.387
- Harry Potter?

01:18:02.387 --> 01:18:03.658
- No, actually, no.

01:18:03.658 --> 01:18:05.013
- What's your UK obsession?

01:18:05.013 --> 01:18:07.793
You can normally pinpoint which
show gets people into like-.

01:18:07.793 --> 01:18:09.385
- "The Beatles."

01:18:09.385 --> 01:18:11.666
- What was the start for your TUB face.

01:18:11.666 --> 01:18:12.957
(indistinct chatter)
- What is she saying?

01:18:12.957 --> 01:18:14.585
- Black battler?

01:18:14.585 --> 01:18:17.441
- Did it start with black battler?

01:18:17.441 --> 01:18:19.131
- No, no, no, I don't know,

01:18:19.131 --> 01:18:21.767
like is The Click Five British?

01:18:21.767 --> 01:18:23.175
What the fuck is The Click Five?

01:18:23.175 --> 01:18:25.079
- Come on, oh man, I feel like-

01:18:25.079 --> 01:18:25.912
- What's is it, is it a TV show?

01:18:25.912 --> 01:18:27.136
- Yeah, a band.

01:18:27.136 --> 01:18:29.318
- After you watched "The
Crown", you were like-

01:18:29.318 --> 01:18:31.619
May, can you look up The Click Five?

01:18:31.619 --> 01:18:33.173
Yeah, after you watched "The
Crown", you were like, "Connor,

01:18:33.173 --> 01:18:34.859
"I'm gonna learn Welsh."
- Are they British?

01:18:34.859 --> 01:18:35.692
What?

01:18:35.692 --> 01:18:36.757
- Yeah, Aki.
- Did she say that?

01:18:36.757 --> 01:18:37.590
- Yeah.

01:18:37.590 --> 01:18:38.548
- Nevermind.

01:18:38.548 --> 01:18:40.333
- They're from Massachusetts.

01:18:40.333 --> 01:18:42.472
I don't know who the hell it was.

01:18:42.472 --> 01:18:44.408
I know, I just listened to a band

01:18:44.408 --> 01:18:46.013
and then it just got
me into British music.

01:18:46.013 --> 01:18:47.769
And then from there I just
got into British culture.

01:18:47.769 --> 01:18:49.709
I just happened to also
be watching Harry Potter

01:18:49.709 --> 01:18:50.542
at the time.

01:18:50.542 --> 01:18:51.847
I guess I might have somewhere in there.

01:18:51.847 --> 01:18:52.904
- Yeah, but then you watched "The Crown."

01:18:52.904 --> 01:18:54.577
And then you told Connor,
I'm gonna learn Welsh.

01:18:54.577 --> 01:18:55.660
- Oh fuck I love "The Crown."

01:18:55.660 --> 01:18:56.891
- You were trying to speak Welsh.

01:18:56.891 --> 01:18:59.396
And I was like, "Whoa,
whoa no one does this."

01:18:59.396 --> 01:19:00.884
- Because it was so pretty.

01:19:00.884 --> 01:19:02.036
Like I was just like, man.

01:19:02.036 --> 01:19:03.461
- Thank you, it is.

01:19:03.461 --> 01:19:05.243
So many people were like,

01:19:05.243 --> 01:19:06.076
"Well, it sounds disgusting."

01:19:06.076 --> 01:19:07.048
And I'm like "You should listen to it."

01:19:07.048 --> 01:19:09.245
- Really, I think Welsh
sounds fucking dope.

01:19:09.245 --> 01:19:11.402
- Yeah I liked, Welsh, I don't know.

01:19:11.402 --> 01:19:12.235
- Best five in the world.

01:19:12.235 --> 01:19:13.276
- Disgusting.
- Best five in the world.

01:19:13.276 --> 01:19:14.482
You've seen our flag?

01:19:14.482 --> 01:19:15.407
It's just a dragon.

01:19:15.407 --> 01:19:16.240
- Fucking UK.

